{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1153847","formula":"C₃₁H₃₂O₂P₂","hill":"C31H32O2P2","elements":["H","C","O","P"],"composition":{"C":31.0,"H":32.0,"O":2.0,"P":2.0},"names":{"en":"DIOP"},"descriptions":{"en":"DIOP (2,3-O-isopropylidene-2,3-dihydroxy-1,4-bis(diphenylphosphino)butane) is an organophosphorus compound that is used as a chiral ligand in asymmetric catalysis. It is a white solid that is soluble in organic solvents. DIOP is prepared from the acetonide of d,l-tartaric acid, which is reduced prior to attachment of the PPh2 substituents.","uk":"DIOP (2,3-O-ізопропіліден-2,3-дигідрокси-1,4-біс(дифенілфосфіно)бутан) — фосфорорганічна сполука, яка використовується як хіральний ліганд в асиметричному каталізі. Це біла тверда речовина, розчинна в органічних розчинниках. DIOP отримують з ацетоніду d,l-винної кислоти, який відновлюють перед приєднанням замісників PPh2."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":122582,"mass":498.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1(OC(C(O1)CP(C2=CC=CC=C2)C3=CC=CC=C3)CP(C4=CC=CC=C4)C5=CC=CC=C5)C","inchikey":"VCHDBLPQYJAQSQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"[5-(diphenylphosphanylmethyl)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl]methyl-diphenylphosphane","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"122582","atoms":67,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.324,"y":-0.403,"z":-0.791,"el":"P"},{"x":-3.324,"y":0.404,"z":-0.79,"el":"P"},{"x":1.175,"y":0.038,"z":-3.081,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.174,"y":-0.03,"z":-3.081,"el":"O"},{"x":0.701,"y":-0.285,"z":-1.768,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.701,"y":0.29,"z":-1.768,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.005,"z":-3.909,"el":"C"},{"x":1.621,"y":0.31,"z":-0.722,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.621,"y":-0.308,"z":-0.723,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.025,"y":1.264,"z":-4.766,"el":"C"},{"x":0.026,"y":-1.251,"z":-4.77,"el":"C"},{"x":3.162,"y":-1.78,"z":0.394,"el":"C"},{"x":4.328,"y":0.791,"z":0.159,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.16